# MANIFEST — file ownership for rnd-project-memory
#
# Draft, 2026-08-17. Derived by reading all 32 files of templates/rnd-project, then revised
# after EXP-2026-08-17-pattern-list-extraction and EXP-2026-08-17-misdirection-recheck.
# See ownership-findings.md for the audit and the experiment records for the corrections.
#
# Format: <layer> <path>
#
#   mechanism  upstream owns it; replaced wholesale on upgrade
#   profile    stack-specific; substituted (but see the note on pre-commit below)
#   scaffold   copied at bootstrap only; upstream revisions never propagate
#   content    project-generated; upstream never reads or writes it
#   norcopy    belongs to the template repository; never copied into a project
#
# .template-hashes ships with a release and carries the sha256 of every mechanism entry below,
# with paths relative to a consumer's repository root. It is deliberately absent from this list:
# a file cannot carry its own hash. MIGRATIONS.md "Cutting a release" regenerates it.
#
# THE HASH LIST MAY CONTAIN ONLY FILES INSTALLED VERBATIM, SUBJECT TO NO TRANSFORMATION.
#
# Not "files nobody is told to edit" — the transformations differ in kind and the consequence is
# the same. A file the install renames can never be found at the path the list names. A file a
# profile substitutes into never matches the hash it shipped with. A file whose placeholders step
# 3 fills is modified before its first commit. In all three the check reports FAILED on a correct
# adoption, on the first line of output an adopter ever sees, and what it teaches is that failing
# checks are normal — which costs more than the check was ever worth.
#
# A mechanism file that is transformed on install carries `# transformed on install` on its line
# below and is excluded from the generated list; nothing else may be. `bootstrap-test.sh` enforces
# this by installing the skeleton and verifying every hashed path survives byte-for-byte, which is
# the criterion restated as an executable test. Three entries violated it before v2.2.0:
# `gitignore.template` (renamed), `.githooks/pre-commit` (substituted into — fixed by moving the
# substitution point out to `.githooks/patterns.profile`), and `ai-sandbox/RATIONALE.md` (carried
# `<PROJECT_NAME>` in its title — fixed by removing it). None was visible to this repository's own
# check.sh, which performs no installation.
#
# There is no general region scope. An earlier draft fenced upstream preambles inside nine files
# and scoped manifest entries to those regions; that was withdrawn — markers serve a tool, and this
# design builds no tool. Rule changes reach projects through ai-sandbox/RULES.md, which is
# mechanism and replaced whole; preamble revisions ride on prose migrations.
#
# ONE EXCEPTION, AND IT IS CONDITIONAL. A file is split into owned regions only where an include
# mechanism is unavailable. If the file can import another file, the AGENTS.md/RULES.md device is
# used instead — a small file the project owns, importing a large one upstream owns.
#
# .gitignore is the only file that qualifies: it is a security control that must also carry the
# project's own lines, and git has no include directive for it (.git/info/exclude and
# core.excludesFile are per-clone and uncommitted, so neither reaches a second machine). Its
# marker splits it; everything from `# ─── UPSTREAM BLOCK` down is upstream's, everything above is
# the project's, and upstream sits last because .gitignore is last-match-wins.
#
# Without the condition, "put a marker in it" becomes the answer every time the choice between
# mechanism and scaffold is unpleasant, and one word per file stops answering "who owns this?".
# bootstrap-test.sh fails the release if a second installed file grows a region marker. See
# ADR-009.

# ─── never copied into an adopting project ───────────────────────────────────
norcopy    README.md
norcopy    ../RND_PROJECT_MEMORY.md
norcopy    ../bootstrap-test.sh

# ─── mechanism: replaced wholesale on upgrade ────────────────────────────────
mechanism  check.sh

# Upstream owns the region below its UPSTREAM BLOCK marker and replaces that region wholesale;
# everything above the marker is the project's and is never touched. It is not scaffold: an
# ignore list is a security control, and `.gitignore` has no include mechanism, so the AGENTS.md
# device — a small project file importing a large upstream one — is unavailable here. Handing the
# whole file to the project would mean a strengthened never-commit pattern could never again reach
# a project already running, which is a regression dressed as a layer change.
mechanism  gitignore.template            # transformed on install
mechanism  ai-sandbox/RULES.md
mechanism  ai-sandbox/RATIONALE.md
mechanism  ai-sandbox/playbooks/session-start.md
mechanism  ai-sandbox/playbooks/checkpoint.md
mechanism  ai-sandbox/playbooks/promote.md
mechanism  ai-sandbox/playbooks/ingest-source.md
mechanism  ai-sandbox/playbooks/run-experiment.md
mechanism  ai-sandbox/playbooks/upgrade-template.md
mechanism  ai-sandbox/sessions/_TEMPLATE.md
mechanism  ai-sandbox/experiments/_TEMPLATE.md
mechanism  ai-sandbox/playbooks/local/_TEMPLATE.md
mechanism  docs/decisions/_TEMPLATE.md
mechanism  docs/techniques/_TEMPLATE.md

# Mechanism, and now genuinely verbatim. A profile used to be substituted into this file
# directly, which put the one check whose failure a later edit cannot repair permanently out of
# step with its own hash. The substitution point moved to .githooks/patterns.profile, read as
# data and never sourced; the core list is inline and cannot go missing. Keeping this file
# hashable matters more than for any other entry: it is the file you most need to know is intact.
mechanism  .githooks/pre-commit

# ─── profile: substituted per stack ──────────────────────────────────────────
profile    ai-sandbox/DATA_ENVIRONMENT.md

# Credential patterns beyond the core, one alternative per line. Deliberately not hashed — it is
# the file the organisation writes. The hook drops blank and comment lines (an empty alternative
# matches every line) and discards the whole file if it does not compile (a malformed pattern
# makes grep exit 2, which reads as "found nothing" and would silently disable the scan).
profile    .githooks/patterns.profile

# ─── scaffold: seeded once, the project's own thereafter ─────────────────────
# The register and index files below carry an upstream preamble above project entries. They
# are scaffold rather than mechanism because a stale preamble does not misdirect: the failure
# mode is missing a newly added rule, not following a false one, and rules that must reach
# existing projects live in RULES.md. See EXP-2026-08-17-misdirection-recheck.
scaffold   AGENTS.md
scaffold   .template-version
scaffold   ai-sandbox/INDEX.md
scaffold   ai-sandbox/CHECKPOINT-thread.md
scaffold   ai-sandbox/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md
scaffold   ai-sandbox/ASSUMPTIONS.md
scaffold   ai-sandbox/SOURCES.md
scaffold   ai-sandbox/CAVEATS.yaml
scaffold   ai-sandbox/PUBLICATIONS.md
scaffold   ai-sandbox/CONFIGURATIONS.md
scaffold   ai-sandbox/sessions/LOG.md
scaffold   ai-sandbox/experiments/LOG.md
scaffold   docs/CLAIMS.md

# Temporary by design — exists only until the 3-week staleness threshold is validated against
# real data, then deleted along with the answer. See its own header and RATIONALE.md.
scaffold   ai-sandbox/STALENESS_LOG.md

# starting shapes for documents the project writes
scaffold   ai-sandbox/ASSISTANT_PROFILE.md
scaffold   docs/problem.md
scaffold   docs/method.md
scaffold   docs/constraints.md
scaffold   docs/glossary.md
scaffold   src/README.md
scaffold   sources/README.md
scaffold   ai-sandbox/results/README.md

# ─── content: project-generated, upstream never touches ──────────────────────
content    ai-sandbox/sessions/*.md
content    ai-sandbox/experiments/EXP-*.md
content    ai-sandbox/CHECKPOINT-*.md
content    ai-sandbox/env/*.md
content    ai-sandbox/results/*.json
content    ai-sandbox/playbooks/local/*.md
content    docs/decisions/ADR-*.md
content    docs/techniques/*.md
content    sources/**
content    src/**
